{"data":"{\"thinking\":{\"type\":\"adaptive\"},\"stream\":true,\"tools\":[{\"description\":\"Read text with one-based inclusive start_line/end_line. Optional max_bytes bounds the read; job reports cap inline output and preserve the full result on disk.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"start_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"end_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]},\"name\":\"read_file\"},{\"description\":\"List immediate entries, sorted by name; directories end with /.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]},\"name\":\"list_directory\"},{\"description\":\"Search files recursively using a regular expression. context_lines defaults to zero. Output uses grep path:line:text and path-line-context with merged windows.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"context_lines\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"pattern\"]},\"name\":\"search_files\"},{\"description\":\"Write text, creating parent directories. Existing files require overwrite:true unless append:true. Append preserves existing content.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"overwrite\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"append\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"content\"]},\"name\":\"write_file\"},{\"description\":\"Replace one exact, unique old_text anchor with new_text. Zero or multiple matches refuse without changing the file; read and provide a more specific anchor.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"old_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"new_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"old_text\",\"new_text\"]},\"name\":\"edit_file\"},{\"description\":\"Start a fresh /bin/sh in a PTY. cwd applies only to this call, relative to the workspace. Merged output and exit_code stay on disk; a running report is a handle, not cancellation. ai_callback_delay is seconds (default 3); pattern matches unseen output; max_output_bytes defaults to 16384.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"cwd\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"command\"]},\"name\":\"run_command\"},{\"description\":\"Wait for a job, including a finished job. Return only unseen output; waiting does not stop execution.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"]},\"name\":\"wait_for_job\"},{\"description\":\"Send a line of input to a running PTY job, then wait. A missing trailing newline is added.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"input\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\",\"input\"]},\"name\":\"send_input\"},{\"description\":\"Kill a job's process group. Go-only work is marked killed but its goroutine cannot be stopped.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"]},\"name\":\"kill_job\"},{\"description\":\"Set one-shot wait/output limits for the very next call, whichever tool it is. That call reports consumption; explicit call arguments override these limits.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[]},\"name\":\"tool_limits\"},{\"description\":\"Checkpoint at a completed micro-goal. Write text with what succeeded, what failed, source locations and next steps. Removes all tool traffic but preserves conversation and this note.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"]},\"name\":\"micro_handoff\"},{\"description\":\"Keep the previous batch of tool results instead of automatic stubbing on supported models. Does not keep results of tools called alongside this call.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{}},\"name\":\"keep_tool_results\"}],\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"max_tokens\":4096,\"system\":\"You are a helpful assistant built from raw HTTP calls in Chapter 1 of The Art of Building AI Coding Agents. Answer briefly.\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I am working on Cedar Lantern (release CL-721). I rejected automatic deletion of imported notes because support needs originals when customers report mistakes. Design: originals stay in an archive; accepted summaries are stored separately, each tagged with its source identifier; if summarization fails, the original stays available. Default retention is 30 days. Cleanup runs only after a completed review, never because of an unrelated request, since cleanup tied to request arrival could delete unreviewed work. Morgan owns archive review, scheduled October 18.\\n\\nOpen for Cedar Lantern: (1) If the 30-day retention expires before the October 18 review finishes, I have not decided whether the original is deleted or held. My reading is that originals stay available until review is done, but the spec doesn't say so; this needs to be written down. (2) Attachments: same archive or a separate one is undecided. It affects retention and review scope and should be settled before October 18. I offered to draft a decision record for either item; that offer is pending.\\n\\nCase two: Harbor Finch deployment rehearsal (diagnostic tag HF-934), owned by Priya, scheduled October 21. Decided: I rejected automatic retry of a database migration after a timeout, because the remote operation may already have committed. The procedure reads the migration ledger before deciding whether a retry is safe. The operator records the exact migration identifier and the measured error, not a guess about success. The rollback package stays available for seven days after deployment. New evidence: a log line said the worker had stopped, but the child process was still alive holding the port. Log messages are not proof of process state, so the rehearsal checks child lifetime directly.\\n\\nUnresolved: whether the migration ledger lives with application data or in a separate control database. Next steps: confirm the ledger location before the October 21 rehearsal, and verify the child-lifetime check is in the rehearsal procedure.\"}]}]}","event":"request"}
